{"name":"Suntan","hex":"#d9b19f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Suntan","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The ship of characters Sunny and Kel from the videogame Omori."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Suntan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sun tanning","blocks":[{"text":"Sun tanning or tanning is the process whereby skin color is darkened or tanned. It is most often a result of exposure to ultraviolet (UV) radiation from sunlight or from artificial sources, such as a tanning lamp found in indoor tanning beds. People who deliberately tan their skin by exposure to the sun engage in a passive recreational activity of sun bathing. Some people use chemical products that can produce a tanning effect without exposure to ultraviolet radiation, known as sunless tanning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Tan_lines_on_human_female_chest.jpg/330px-Tan_lines_on_human_female_chest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun_tanning"},{"title":"Suntan (apple)","blocks":[{"text":"Suntan is an English cultivar of domesticated apple that have earned the Award of Garden Merit by the Royal Horticultural Society in 1999."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Malus-Suntan.jpg/330px-Malus-Suntan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suntan_(apple)"},{"title":"Suntan (2016 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Suntan is a 2016 Greek drama film directed by Argyris Papadimitropoulos, from a screenplay by Papadimitropoulos and Syllas Tzoumerkas. It stars Makis Papadimitriou as a middle-aged general practitioner on a resort island who becomes obsessed with a young female patient. The film premiered at the International Film Festival Rotterdam on February 2, 2016, and was theatrically released in Greece on March 31, 2016. Critical response for Suntan has been positive."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ca/Suntan_2016_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suntan_(2016_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Skin_tanning.JPG/500px-Skin_tanning.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Skin_tanning.JPG/1280px-Skin_tanning.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Skin_tanning.JPG/500px-Skin_tanning.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sun tanned arm showing browner skin where it has been exposed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkin_tanning.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Photoaging.jpg/330px-Photoaging.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Photoaging.jpg/330px-Photoaging.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photoaging of a woman","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhotoaging.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Melanin_production_as_a_result_of_tanning.jpg/500px-Melanin_production_as_a_result_of_tanning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Melanin_production_as_a_result_of_tanning.jpg/500px-Melanin_production_as_a_result_of_tanning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cross-sectional view showing skin tone becoming darker due to the production of more melanin to overcome DNA damage caused by UV radiation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMelanin_production_as_a_result_of_tanning.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Sun_burn.JPG/500px-Sun_burn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Sun_burn.JPG/500px-Sun_burn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sunburn peeling","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASun_burn.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Disappearing_sun_tan.jpg/500px-Disappearing_sun_tan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Disappearing_sun_tan.jpg/500px-Disappearing_sun_tan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Disappearing sun tan, revealing the individual's naturally light-colored skin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADisappearing_sun_tan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Monet_Umbrella.JPG/500px-Monet_Umbrella.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Monet_Umbrella.JPG/1280px-Monet_Umbrella.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Monet_Umbrella.JPG/500px-Monet_Umbrella.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"La promenade (1875) by Claude Monet. At that time in the West, the upper social class used parasols, long sleeves and hats to avoid sunlight's tanning effects.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonet_Umbrella.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/715px-Sunbedoff_large.jpg/500px-715px-Sunbedoff_large.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte